> box, unused (/dev/sdb). Problem: It won't find the tulip NIC!!
> 
> Is there anything I have to do before it finds that? I tried tulip and
> tulip_old with the default settings.

That TULIP is on the EISA bus (note the first vmunix: line above), and
thus you need the DE422 driver, named "depca".

As for BSD-style partitioning, leave ~5MB before the first partition for
the bootstrap to be installed into.

Good luck.

